1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,620
Good afternoon, Dreamtime Travel.

2
00:00:02,620 --> 00:00:03,930
How can I help you?

3
00:00:03,930 --> 00:00:04,621
Oh hello.

4
00:00:04,621 --> 00:00:08,770
I'm interested in the holidays you offer along the coast near here.

5
00:00:08,770 --> 00:00:09,136
Yes.

6
00:00:09,136 --> 00:00:11,700
We operate several tours up the coast.

7
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:14,630
Where in particular did you want to go?

8
00:00:14,630 --> 00:00:18,971
Well, I like the sound of the holiday that mentioned whales.

9
00:00:18,971 --> 00:00:20,550
Was it 'Whale Watching'?

10
00:00:20,550 --> 00:00:20,940
Oh,

11
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:22,893
that's our Whale Watch Experience.

12
00:00:22,893 --> 00:00:28,360
It's very popular and it's based in a lovely little town with nice beaches.

13
00:00:28,360 --> 00:00:29,055
Oh right,

14
00:00:29,055 --> 00:00:31,140
and how long does it last?

15
00:00:31,140 --> 00:00:36,700
It's two days-that includes four hours' travel time each way from here.

16
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:40,481
Good, I don't want to be away any longer than that.

17
00:00:40,481 --> 00:00:42,200
So is that by coach?

18
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:43,626
Actually it's by minibus.

19
00:00:43,626 --> 00:00:48,619
We like to keep those tours small and personal so we don't take a

20
00:00:48,619 --> 00:00:50,045
whole coachload of people.

21
00:00:50,045 --> 00:00:55,037
In fact, we only take up to fifteen people on this tour, although we

22
00:00:55,037 --> 00:00:57,890
do run it with just twelve or thirteen.

23
00:00:57,890 --> 00:00:58,601
Oh, right.

24
00:00:58,601 --> 00:01:01,090
So do you run these tours often?

25
00:01:01,090 --> 00:01:03,534
Well it depends on the time of year.

26
00:01:03,534 --> 00:01:07,810
Of course in peak times like the summer holidays we do them every weekend,

27
00:01:07,810 --> 00:01:11,170
but at the moment it's usually once a month at most.

28
00:01:11,170 --> 00:01:13,110
And when is the next one going?

29
00:01:13,110 --> 00:01:15,544
Mmm, let me see.

30
00:01:15,544 --> 00:01:22,846
Um, there's one in three weeks' time which is April the 18th,

31
00:01:22,846 --> 00:01:29,540
and then we don't have another one until June the 2nd.

32
00:01:29,540 --> 00:01:30,360
All right,

33
00:01:30,360 --> 00:01:33,640
and is April a good time to go?

34
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:34,301
Pretty good.

35
00:01:34,301 --> 00:01:37,608
Though the really good time is later in the year.

36
00:01:37,608 --> 00:01:42,238
I have to say though that the whale sighting is only one of the

37
00:01:42,238 --> 00:01:43,230
many things offered.

38
00:01:43,230 --> 00:01:44,000
Really?

39
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:44,425
Yes.

40
00:01:44,425 --> 00:01:48,250
The hotel itself where you stay has great facilities.

41
00:01:48,250 --> 00:01:49,950
It's called The Pallisades.

42
00:01:49,950 --> 00:01:51,650
The Paris what?

43
00:01:51,650 --> 00:01:56,676
NO, it's actually The Pallisades, P-A-L-L-I-S-A-D-E-S.

44
00:01:56,676 --> 00:02:02,540
It's right on the main beach there.

45
00:02:02,540 --> 00:02:03,530
Oh, I see.

46
00:02:03,530 --> 00:02:07,861
All of the rooms have nice views and the food is really good there

47
00:02:07,861 --> 00:02:08,170
too.

48
00:02:08,170 --> 00:02:11,140
Oh right.

49
00:02:11,140 --> 00:02:13,129
And what about the other things?

50
00:02:13,129 --> 00:02:13,791
You know,

51
00:02:13,791 --> 00:02:15,780
that are included in the price.

52
00:02:15,780 --> 00:02:17,853
Oh, there are lots of things.

53
00:02:17,853 --> 00:02:22,690
If you don't want to do the whale watch cruise, your guide will take

54
00:02:22,690 --> 00:02:27,528
anyone who is interested either on a bushwalk through the national park near the

55
00:02:27,528 --> 00:02:27,873
hotel,

56
00:02:27,873 --> 00:02:30,292
and there's no extra charge for that,

57
00:02:30,292 --> 00:02:32,020
or on a fishing trip.

58
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:34,093
That's an extra $12 I think.

59
00:02:34,093 --> 00:02:38,930
And there's also a reptile park in town-that costs more or less the same.

60
00:02:38,930 --> 00:02:41,680
No, I think I'd prefer whales to snakes.

61
00:02:41,680 --> 00:02:41,990
Yeah.

62
00:02:41,990 --> 00:02:46,950
And if you just want to relax you are free to sit by the hotel pool

63
00:02:46,950 --> 00:02:48,500
or go down the beach.

64
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:48,810
Oh,

65
00:02:48,810 --> 00:02:51,600
and they also have tennis courts at the hotel,

66
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:54,700
but you have to pay for those by the hour.

67
00:02:54,700 --> 00:02:59,040
But there are table tennis tables downstairs and they're part of the accommodation package.

68
00:02:59,040 --> 00:03:00,590
Just speak to your guide.

69
00:03:00,590 --> 00:03:02,080
Well that sounds good.

70
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:05,060
So how much is the basic tour price?

71
00:03:05,060 --> 00:03:12,911
At this time of year it's usually around $300 but let me check.

72
00:03:12,911 --> 00:03:15,930
Er...oh, it's actually $280.

73
00:03:15,930 --> 00:03:19,070
And the next tour, are there any places on that one?

74
00:03:19,070 --> 00:03:21,210
How many people is it for?

75
00:03:21,210 --> 00:03:22,360
There are two of us.

76
00:03:22,360 --> 00:03:22,742
Yes,

77
00:03:22,742 --> 00:03:24,270
that should be fine.

78
00:03:24,270 --> 00:03:29,620
Can I just mention that we require all bookings to be made at least

79
00:03:29,620 --> 00:03:33,440
fourteen days before you travel to avoid cancellations of tours.

80
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:38,790
And if you cancel within seven days of departure you will have to pay

81
00:03:38,790 --> 00:03:40,700
50% of your total booking.

82
00:03:40,700 --> 00:03:41,630
OK.

83
00:03:41,630 --> 00:03:46,670
And you also need to pay a 20% deposit at the time of booking.

84
00:03:46,670 --> 00:03:48,670
Can I pay that by credit card?

85
00:03:48,670 --> 00:03:49,930
Yes, you can.

86
00:03:49,930 --> 00:03:52,646
All right, what I'll do is I'll talk to my partner

87
00:03:52,646 --> 00:03:53,880
and get back to you.

88
00:03:53,880 --> 00:03:54,252
Fine.

89
00:03:54,252 --> 00:03:59,465
So I'll make a provisional booking, shall I?-Two for the Whale Watch Experience.

90
00:03:59,465 --> 00:04:04,678
Let me issue you with a customer reference number for when you call back.

91
00:04:04,678 --> 00:04:06,540
Do you have a pen?

92
00:04:06,540 --> 00:04:07,280
Yes.

93
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:11,385
OK, it's three nine seven, four five, T.

94
00:04:11,385 --> 00:04:13,437
That's T for tango.

95
00:04:13,437 --> 00:04:19,081
When you call back, ask to speak to the Tour Manager,

96
00:04:19,081 --> 00:04:20,620
that's me, Tracy.

97
00:04:20,620 --> 00:04:22,130
Fine, I will.
